{"lines":[{"t":"Test 3","h":0.01527527448094923,"y":0.060676316109034123,"w":0.053911482493082682,"c":1,"x":0.086366057591502052},{"x":0.38408304474906346,"w":0.12110726674397781,"y":0.10755813924167601,"h":0.01744186102384615,"c":1,"t":"READING"},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.088235294339718093,"y":0.18459302301809943,"w":0.25778546651204426,"h":0.014534884186538477},{"y":0.22078376516008635,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","h":0.019041816198884343,"x":0.088235288148470092,"w":0.70588236490885414,"c":1},{"h":0.017441861023846039,"y":0.24127906947486344,"x":0.08823529128224436,"c":1,"t":"Passage 1 below.","w":0.14532872517903647},{"x":0.33391003796819435,"y":0.28052325604410933,"c":1,"h":0.026334686492855752,"t":"Saving the saiga","w":0.23183390299479162},{"w":0.63667821248372403,"h":0.019020456296735211,"t":"The saiga, a species of antelope native to Central Asia, once roamed the vast","c":1,"x":0.088235288136256473,"y":0.3240027994835678},{"c":1,"t":"grasslands of this region in enormous herds, many millions strong. Regrettably, such","x":0.088178282755960707,"y":0.34124284227765878,"w":0.69215454101562501,"h":0.020699385582274576},{"y":0.35880526610733665,"w":0.72337738037109378,"c":1,"t":"spectacular sights are a thing of the past. Today, the saiga is largely confined to a single","x":0.086418882141212336,"h":0.022470958755097969},{"x":0.088171670683867998,"h":0.019903201669809079,"c":1,"y":0.37777895726235822,"w":0.67659459431966151,"t":"country: Kazakhstan. This country is estimated to be home to well over 90% of the"},{"h":0.022764845274811152,"w":0.71643925984700529,"t":"global saiga population, with Russia, Mongolia and Uzbekistan accounting for the rest.","x":0.088124585091571339,"y":0.39541163741212582,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"The saiga is perfectly adapted to the tough conditions of the remote wilderness of the","y":0.43224796638240104,"x":0.088170721382265643,"w":0.71639795939127604,"h":0.020397538651612535},{"x":0.088177464375134296,"w":0.72329416910807287,"c":1,"t":"steppes of Central Asia. One such adaptation is its bizarre bulbous nose, which enables","h":0.020453236168126665,"y":0.45059960519702913},{"t":"the animal to survive the extreme seasonal temperature swings of the region. The","x":0.08816177004167855,"w":0.67488499959309889,"h":0.020886512633551346,"y":0.46896459659253042,"c":1},{"y":0.4876368106855633,"w":0.69043741861979169,"x":0.088167326831526033,"c":1,"t":"swollen nostrils of the nose serve several purposes: they filter out dust and cool the","h":0.019716758674637624},{"t":"blood during hot, dry summers, and they warm the cold air before it enters the saiga's","h":0.021286759533358235,"c":1,"y":0.50527068506244943,"w":0.71636815388997399,"x":0.088185159424430892},{"x":0.08644006746945801,"w":0.70775660196940104,"c":1,"h":0.022728215905650662,"t":"lungs in winter. Other seasonal adaptations include a heavy winter coat that the saiga","y":0.52312825651525885},{"t":"sheds when the weather warms up.","w":0.29431994120279947,"c":1,"y":0.54412586426116971,"x":0.088148133030089282,"h":0.01702119922037304},{"c":1,"t":"Despite these superb adaptations to harsh conditions, the saiga has no defence","x":0.089965409809963287,"y":0.57977606731369657,"w":0.65743942260742194,"h":0.019061141951756566},{"h":0.020913318957041183,"x":0.088145813810330834,"y":0.59686062349454305,"t":"against the threats posed by humans. It was almost driven to extinction by hunters in","w":0.70259780883789069,"c":1},{"y":0.61554544174352932,"c":1,"w":0.7232887776692708,"h":0.020099581163858793,"t":"the 19th century. Legal protection ensured its survival for a while, and numbers steadily","x":0.088184852194063787},{"x":0.088235284913818365,"y":0.63505948221309572,"c":1,"h":0.017556797131697888,"t":"recovered throughout most of the 20th century. But the respite was only temporary.","w":0.69723185221354167},{"c":1,"x":0.088235296399376842,"w":0.70069203694661453,"t":"In the ten years following the break-up of the former Soviet Union in 1991, over 95%","y":0.65255423353911735,"h":0.018957394332298483},{"y":0.66942478894525226,"h":0.021372373993368332,"c":1,"w":0.68699010213216138,"t":"of the global population was lost - one of the fastest examples of species loss ever","x":0.089892042737730174},{"w":0.20242214202880857,"h":0.017505940062921277,"c":1,"x":0.088235295737456837,"t":"recorded for a mammal.","y":0.69034289741253252},{"w":0.6989619445800781,"h":0.017494751574527623,"t":"The dramatic decline during this decade was due to illegal poaching on an industrial","c":1,"x":0.089965394454269099,"y":0.72673198020072127},{"t":"scale. Male saiga are a particular target, because their horns are highly prized by","h":0.021779382036981931,"y":0.74274781472567086,"c":1,"w":0.66797251383463552,"x":0.088154621581084933},{"t":"traditional medicine practitioners. Poaching reached epidemic levels after misguided","w":0.70242212931315107,"x":0.088235309089099018,"h":0.020441396324846428,"c":1,"y":0.76017441869173685},{"y":0.77979981106389296,"t":"conservationists tried to relieve the pressure on threatened African rhinos by actively","x":0.089891240515932697,"w":0.70083480834960943,"h":0.020745649130883281,"c":1},{"x":0.089965402684109491,"h":0.017532386005633893,"c":1,"y":0.80087209274132598,"t":"encouraging the use of saiga horns in traditional medicine as an alternative to those","w":0.69377161661783859},{"t":"of rhinos. Male saiga were aimost wiped out, leading to a population crash from which","h":0.021515772174170555,"y":0.8165992848292587,"w":0.71464045206705729,"c":1,"x":0.089915268591278824},{"w":0.44636678059895835,"h":0.017584260149048792,"c":1,"t":"the species has been struggling to recover ever since.","y":0.83720930204181199,"x":0.089965398550089185},{"c":1,"h":0.019049953463362801,"t":"Another threat to the survival of the saiga is loss of habitat, as a result of agricultural","w":0.69723185221354167,"x":0.089965388811924923,"y":0.87193841859282373},{"x":0.089965391073313958,"y":0.88943317026079483,"t":"expansion and human settlement. Physical barriers such as railways, pipelines and","h":0.018997062245309504,"c":1,"w":0.67474049886067711},{"t":"fences can block the seasonal migration routes of this transboundary species. In the","c":1,"h":0.018998079319947903,"y":0.90832750180816846,"x":0.089965395962584294,"w":0.69204152425130205},{"x":0.089882010346313448,"w":0.49496754964192707,"h":0.021196275261251007,"t":"worst cases, herds may starve to death after being trapped.","c":1,"y":0.92695437010392534},{"t":"60","x":0.089965398292816939,"y":0.96075581402314469,"w":0.022491348584493004,"h":0.013081395100512871,"c":1}],"h":2857,"w":2400}